  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 425f70a701d340949ad6110bc3f45d64, type: 3}
  m_Name: TopDownFrictionInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WorkshopExampleInfo
  m_Scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: 35712a3bd33b4a34fbb17c272d533100, type: 3}
  m_ScenePath: Assets/Examples/TopDownFriction/TopDownFriction.unity
  m_ExampleName: Top Down Friction
  m_Category: Joints
  m_Purpose: "Demonstrates top-down friction with the relative joint. In a top-down view there is no gravity pressing a body onto the ground, so ordinary friction does nothing. A relative joint to the ground with a limited maximum force and torque resists movement and spin the way friction would.\nThe shapes on the table slide to a stop and stop spinning instead of drifting forever."
  m_Controls: "Explode: sets off an explosion that throws the shapes around.\nMax Force and Max Torque: how much force and torque each friction joint can resist. They act on the shapes where they are."
  m_Description: Demonstrating using the RelativeJoint to achieve "top down" friction.
